# Local Claude state (project skills at .claude/skills/ ARE tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Screenshots from ORBS_CAPTURE / F12
orbs-screenshot.png

# The parse trace from F6, in either frontend. Its sibling above was ignored and
# this never was — which went unnoticed while exactly one build could produce it.
orbs-parse.tsv

# The save, from either build. Its two siblings above are ignored and it would
# be the third thing a `git status` in a played-in checkout kept offering.
orbs-save.toml
orbs-save.toml.writing
# ...and the other five slots the menu can keep, plus the one an unreadable save
# is set aside as. Slot 1 is the line above; 2-6 sit beside it.
orbs-save-*.toml
orbs-save-*.toml.writing
orbs-save*.toml.unreadable
# ...and what the player chose about the orb itself, which is kept beside the
# saves and is per-machine for the same reason they are: it is not a tower, and
# nobody else's copy of it means anything.
orbs-settings.toml
assets/online/

# Trained weights are a build artefact of `orbs-augury --example train`, not
# source. 1.4 MB of floats that change on every run would make a diff useless
# and a history heavy; the trainer is deterministic, so the recipe is what is
# kept. Shipping will embed a chosen artefact deliberately (DESIGN.md §19).
crates/orbs-augury/weights/
